    "teacher_markdown": "### **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n**Students may describe what is shown but not what is hidden**\r\n\r\nSome students will write a result message like \"3 results found\" without explaining why other opportunities are missing. Encourage them to think from the user's perspective by asking: **\"If you only saw these jobs, would you know what was filtered out?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nresultCount.textContent =\r\n  \"Showing bikeable opportunities within 3 miles. Farther opportunities are hidden. \" +\r\n  results.length +\r\n  \" results found.\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students understand that transparency includes both what is included and what is excluded.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may place the transparency message before filtering finishes**\r\n\r\nStudents may update `resultCount` before the results array is complete, leading to incorrect counts. Encourage them to trace the order of execution by asking: **\"When does the program know how many results it found?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant pattern:\r\n```javascript\r\nrenderResults(results);\r\n\r\nresultCount.textContent = \"... \" + results.length + \" results found.\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe transparency message should come after the filtering is complete.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may write labels that repeat the button text instead of explaining the filter**\r\n\r\nStudents often write messages like \"Bikeable filter applied.\" Encourage them to make the message more informative by asking: **\"Does the label explain the rule and its impact on the results?\"**\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n```javascript\r\n\"Showing entry-level opportunities that require 1 year of experience or less. Jobs requiring more experience are hidden.\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students communicate both the filter rule and its effect.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may test only whether the filter works**\r\n\r\nStudents may verify that the correct jobs appear but not read the transparency message. Encourage them to evaluate both the data and the explanation by asking: **\"If you were a first-time user, would this message help you understand why you're seeing these results?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant pattern:\r\n```javascript\r\nresultCount.textContent =\r\n  \"... \" + results.length + \" results found.\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis reinforces that transparency is part of the user experience, not just an extra feature."
  },
